+### Space usage queries
+
+If space reservation is enabled (`xrootd.enable.space-reservation`), the
+door answers space queries (`kXR_Qspace`) for paths that are associated
+with a space reservation through the `WriteToken` directory tag. The
+reply reports the size of the reservation and the space still available
+in it, using the same format as xrootd's oss plugin. This allows
+clients to see the capacity of a space reservation, e.g.:
+
+```console-user
+xrdfs door.example.org spaceinfo /data/cms
+|Path:               /data/cms
+|Total:              1099511627776
+|Free:               274877906944
+|Used:               824633720832
+|Largest free chunk: 274877906944
+```
+
+and makes `df` show the same values on a directory mounted with
+`xrootdfs`. For paths without a `WriteToken` tag the query fails.
+
